Filed by langertha-llm-advisor, 2026-09-01. Docs read 2026-09-01, no live calls.

## Deadline: 26 days

Every Perplexity Sonar doc page now carries the banner, verbatim:

  "Sonar Chat Completions is now Agent API. Sonar will be supported until **September 27, 2026**."

`Engine::Perplexity::default_model` is `sonar`. The engine's model list
(`sonar`, `sonar-pro`, `sonar-deep-research`, `sonar-reasoning-pro`) still matches the docs enum
exactly -- the engine is accurate TODAY and stops working in under four weeks.

Sources (read 2026-09-01): docs.perplexity.ai/api-reference/sonar-post ,
docs.perplexity.ai/docs/sonar/models.md , /docs/sonar/features.md

## What replaces it, and why neither successor is a drop-in

Perplexity has split the surface in two, and BOTH invalidate a Langertha assumption:

1. **Agent API** -- the named successor to Sonar Chat Completions. Non-OpenAI request shape.
   `Engine::Perplexity` extends `OpenAIBase`; if the Agent API is where search-augmented chat
   lives after 2026-09-27, that is a wire-envelope change (ADR 0006 dialect axis), not a URL swap.
2. **Router API** -- `POST /router/v1/chat/completions`, full OpenAI shape INCLUDING named
   `tool_choice`, `allowed_tools`, `parallel_tool_calls` (default true), and
   `response_format.json_schema` which "always runs in strict mode". **Private preview,
   email-gated.** Catalog is six open-weight models (`perplexity/kimi-k3`,
   `deepseek-v4-flash-0731`, `glm-5.2`, `glm-5.3`, two nemotron), i.e. it is a routing product,
   not Sonar.
   Source: docs.perplexity.ai/api-reference/gateway-chat-completions-post , /docs/router/models.md

**This matters beyond one engine.** Perplexity is the single load-bearing example behind ADR 0005
rewrite direction 1 -- "forced named tool -> response_format" fires on
`!supports('tool_choice_named') && supports('response_format_json_schema')`, and Perplexity is
the only engine in the distribution that hits it (`t/78_engine_capabilities.t:38` asserts exactly
that). If Perplexity's successor surface gains named tool_choice (the Router API has it), the
rewrite direction loses its only real-world consumer and ADR 0005 needs a note saying so.

Also confirmed still true and NOT to be "fixed": Sonar genuinely has no tool calling. `tools` and
`tool_choice` appear nowhere in the Sonar API reference or guides, and the repo's own live 400
("Tool calling is not supported for this model") stands.

## Second, smaller drift on the same engine

`Engine::Perplexity` does `delete $caps->{reasoning_effort}` in its `around engine_capabilities`
(Perplexity.pm:92-96). The current Sonar API reference documents `reasoning_effort` as an accepted
body parameter with values `minimal|low|medium|high`. So that correction is now itself stale --
the flag should come back (it is also the kind of thing `sonar-reasoning-pro` exists for).
`delete $caps->{prompt_cache_key}` in the same block was not re-checked and may or may not still
hold.

## Suggested action

1. Decide before 2026-09-27 whether Langertha follows Perplexity to the Agent API (new wire
   envelope), to the Router API (needs preview access), or deprecates `Engine::Perplexity`.
   Doing nothing means the engine breaks on that date.
2. Independently and cheaply: restore `reasoning_effort` on Perplexity, and re-verify
   `prompt_cache_key`.
3. Note in ADR 0005 that rewrite direction 1's exemplar is time-limited, whichever way (1) goes.
